From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: hevc: an interrupt before anything is
 parsed is no error

The microcode also interrupts with dec_status 0, before it has parsed
anything: for its debug messages through DEBUG_REG1, which Amlogic's
driver clears. The driver took such an interrupt for a fault and aborted
the session. With CMA full of movable pages, a 4K HEVC Main10 session's
CAPTURE buffers took a moment to migrate in, and the session aborted on
one of these at its start.

Ignore an interrupt with nothing parsed, as VP9 already does, and clear
the debug tag. Any other unknown status still aborts.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 vdec/codec_hevc.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vdec/codec_hevc.c b/vdec/codec_hevc.c
--- a/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -2298,6 +2298,12 @@
 		finish_yield = true;
 		goto unlock;
 	}
+	if (!dec_status) {
+		dev_dbg(core->dev_dec, "dec_status 0, debug tag %08X: nothing parsed, ignored\n",
+			amvdec_read_dos(core, DEBUG_REG1));
+		amvdec_write_dos(core, DEBUG_REG1, 0);
+		goto unlock;
+	}
 	if (dec_status != HEVC_SLICE_SEGMENT_DONE) {
 		dev_err(core->dev_dec, "Unrecognized dec_status: %08X\n",
 			dec_status);
-- 
